  "Question": "What is the value of the following product?\n\n\\[\\dfrac{3 \\times 5}{9 \\times 11} \\times \\dfrac{7 \\times 9 \\times 11}{3 \\times 5 \\times 7}\\]",
  "Question Type": "text",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "\\(1\\)",
    "B": "\\(0\\)",
    "C": "\\(49\\)",
    "D": "\\(\\dfrac{1}{49}\\)",
    "E": "\\(50\\)"
  },
  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Correct Answer": "A",
  "Solution": "Multiplying the fractions puts all the numerator factors together and all the denominator factors together:\n\\[\n\\frac{3\\times5}{9\\times11}\\times\\frac{7\\times9\\times11}{3\\times5\\times7}\n=\\frac{3\\times5\\times7\\times9\\times11}{9\\times11\\times3\\times5\\times7}.\n\\]\nEach factor occurs once in the numerator and once in the denominator. All are nonzero, so they cancel, leaving \\(1\\), choice \\(\\mathrm{A}\\).",
